00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.095
So what is tracing
and why do you need tracing?

12
00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:33.266
Tracing basically means
recording the inputs and outputs

13
00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.269
of the intermediate function
inside your AI program.

14
00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.339
And the capture is a hierarchical calling
stack

15
00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.442
like module A cost module B. GenAI

16
00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.445
applications can be very complex
internally

17
00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:48.648
while only the final output is exposed.

18
00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:52.419
So when something is going off, it's
hard to trace back to the root cause.

19
00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:55.422
For example, if you have built a DSPy

20
00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:58.425
program consisting of five submodules.

21
00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:03.396
Now, if one LM calls fails due to not
being able to understand the prompt,

22
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:07.901
even though the DSPy provides
inspect history to check LM calls,

23
00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.202
it's hard to trace back.

24
00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:14.202
Tracing provides an easy way
for interpretability and debugging.

25
00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:19.808
And what is MLflow?
MLflow is an open-source AI ops package

26
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.349
that streamlines
your GenAI app development.

27
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:28.054
MLflow helps with a full lifecycle
of building GenAI applications,

28
00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:32.192
ensuring that its face is traceable
and reproducible.

29
00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:36.062
Both MLFlow Server and appliance
are fully open sourced.

30
00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.997
You can easily set it up.

31
00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:41.468
To get started by tracing a DSPy
with MLflow.

32
00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:45.672
You only need to add a
one line to a program which is MLflow

33
00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.908
dot DSPy dot autolog. Or simply MLflow dot autolog.

34
00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:53.146
After that,
your program will be automatically traced

35
00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.182
and the trace will be saved
in the MLflow server.

36
00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:59.018
that you can access point in time
after being generated.

